Z||000000||Thor||04-09-2001||09:51 PM||||SPRING FEVER IN MINNESOTA !!! I'm spending the month restoring some of my brake and suspension ellements on my 86GT 5 speed. Replaced the struts and shocks,restored the rear callipers and now on to the front rotors.  Here's my question. When I bought the rotors they were rotor/hub assembly units. Is this correct? I'm in the cities and the car is in Wisconsin so I can't check till I go up to work on it next week. When I checked the GM manual it did not state spicifically that this indeed is the correct configuration.  If it is I'll replace the bearings as well. By the way I'v seen posts were people were spending a TON of money on rotors. I called around and found them at Pronto Auto Parts for $18.50 each for rear and $36.00 each for front.  Thanks for any help on this matter in advance. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||ka4nkf||04-09-2001||10:03 PM||||Thor<BR>The front assembly is rotor/hub assembly units. Replace the bearings and races and you will be in business. Good Luck.<BR>Don||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||04-10-2001||12:22 AM||||New hub assys. come with races installed. Just get bearings and seals and you'll be good to go!||||reg||1
